WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:13.305
One of the ideas behind Servant is that

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:17.601
we never leave
the brownstone on Spruce Street.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.980
And that was the conceit, give it
this kind of suffocating feeling.

00:00:23.065 --> 00:00:25.359
So episode one of season three,

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:28.237
where Leanne goes outside
for the first time,

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:31.031
is something I really
looked forward to directing

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:36.161
because it's a very Hitchcockian
sequence of paranoia.

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:38.413
It's her trying to overcome

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:42.543
her almost crippling anxiety
about going outside.

00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:45.838
From the beginning,
when you see her from behind,

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:47.297
she's gathering her strength.

00:00:47.381 --> 00:00:50.092
She wanted this life.
She wanted to stay in this brownstone,

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.970
but she knows that
something dark's coming for her.

00:00:53.178 --> 00:00:55.639
So, can she even enjoy this anymore?

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.725
All she's ever wanted to be
is this normal girl in this family.

00:00:59.101 --> 00:01:01.311
Can I just take a walk down the street?

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:06.275
We had to go through the wall,
and we actually did go through the wall,

00:01:06.358 --> 00:01:09.820
to kind of come on the outside
and then dip down and then zoom in.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.157
This is a much harder shot than it looks.

00:01:16.326 --> 00:01:18.287
All the sound effects explode,

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.789
and the room is filling up
with her paranoia.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:26.086
Just each step, with this
wide-angle lens, this sense of like,

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:29.965
 it's very hard to walk, just keep going,
and her forcing herself to go forward.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:33.051
Leanne keeps looking around
over her shoulder

00:01:33.135 --> 00:01:35.554
to see if anybody's gonna
run up behind her and attack her.

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:37.222
And we're doing very close shots,

00:01:37.306 --> 00:01:40.976
so you can see her face is warping
with how wide our lens is.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:43.020
And it's like, keep getting
closer to her, closer to her,

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.814
so she's feeling suffocated,
even though she's outside.

00:01:47.608 --> 00:01:51.653
There's this stranger
that looks awfully like Uncle George,

00:01:51.737 --> 00:01:54.364
the person that attacked her
in season two.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.701
And she's watching him and going,
"Why is he standing there?"

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.912
Meanwhile, Julian's trying
to break up with her

00:01:59.995 --> 00:02:01.205
over her shoulder.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.499
She's sick of being told what to do.

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:07.419
And she finds her strength here.
This is what this frame is.

00:02:07.503 --> 00:02:11.423
The walking stops, and now
she's gonna go and be a different person.

00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:14.051
-And now it's time I think we--
-No.

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:24.603
She feels foolish, and she's like,
"I can't be normal out here."

00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:28.899
And so she grabs the baby,
and she's very upset.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.193
Julian's outside, and then you see...

00:02:31.318 --> 00:02:32.069
Boom...

00:02:35.364 --> 00:02:37.282
the house starting to fall apart.

00:02:37.366 --> 00:02:39.201
The house and her are kinda tied,

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.870
and as she gets angry
and feels certain emotions,

00:02:41.954 --> 00:02:44.248
the house manifests that.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.586
I found this episode
so scary and unnerving,

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:54.466
and leans into the things
that I'm passionate about,

00:02:54.550 --> 00:02:58.720
which is paranoia and suspense,
and like, kinda that wink

00:02:58.804 --> 00:03:03.016
as we kind of tumble into
darker and darker things for Leanne.

